 ## Background
-The family originates from the need to bypass the computational bottleneck and fragility of Structure-from-Motion (SfM) in 3D Gaussian Splatting. Traditional 3DGS requires dense, accurate camera poses, which are often unavailable or noisy in casual capture scenarios. Methods like [pixelSplat](6464-pixelsplat.md) introduced feed-forward architectures to predict Gaussian primitives directly from image pairs, addressing local minima issues through differentiable sampling [S1, unofficial]. Subsequent works like [InstantSplat](6136-instantsplat.md) and [AnySplat](6137-anysplat.md) leveraged foundation models (MASt3R, VGGT) for geometry priors or joint pose-primitive prediction to enable pose-free reconstruction from sparse or uncalibrated views [S1, unofficial]. The [VS-Splat](6137-anysplat.md) extension further adapted these feed-forward approaches to handle noisy camera poses by modifying input feature dimensions to match existing pose-aware baselines like SHARE [S1, unofficial].
+The family originates from the need to generalize 3D Gaussian Splatting beyond single-scene optimization, which is computationally expensive and requires accurate initial poses [6464-pixelsplat.md]. Early work like pixelSplat [6464-pixelsplat.md] introduced feed-forward architectures to predict Gaussian primitives directly from image pairs, addressing the local minima issues of traditional splatting. Subsequent developments like InstantSplat [6136-instantsplat.md] and AnySplat [6137-anysplat.md] incorporated foundation model priors (e.g., MASt3R, VGGT) to enable pose-free reconstruction from sparse or uncalibrated views, significantly reducing training time to seconds [S1, unofficial]. Joint Pose Optimization [6888-joint-pose-optimization.md] provides an alternative by treating poses as learnable parameters rather than predicting them via a network. These methods are used in generalizable novel view synthesis, 3D object reconstruction from sparse views, and applications requiring real-time rendering from casual captures [6464-pixelsplat.md, S1].
 
